sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch03-11> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The struggle for existence is almost always most severe between individuals of the same species, because they live in the same places, need the same food and face the same dangers; between varieties of a species it is nearly as severe.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Struggle is most severe between members of the same species";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter III, “Struggle for Existence”; section “Struggle for life most severe between individuals and varieties of the same species; often severe between species of the same genus”. Scope: all organisms, including varieties of cultivated plants and domestic animals"
}
